Lantern Woodland: A/B/C native viewport sample source kit

Each variant contains the preserved 1536x1024 native scene, exact generation prompt, provenance metadata, and a presentation-only hero160 composite.

Rebuild: install Pillow, then run python review/build_contexts.py woodland
All image input paths are relative and the original transparent hero is bundled. Pillow and a system font are the only runtime dependencies; the script falls back to Pillow default text if DejaVu is unavailable.

Hero compositing is deterministic raster compositing, with Lanczos hero resize and a small added grounding shadow. Native scenes are untouched; no full-map expansion, AI upscale or generated repainting is included. The comparison sheet downscales presentation previews.

No camera geometry, collision, engine scale or occlusion validation is claimed. Scenery is baked into these viewport art-direction samples.
